{
  "type": "mod",
  "id": 2394,
  "hub_id": null,
  "guid": "com.ozen.instantinsurance",
  "name": "Instant Insurance",
  "slug": "instant-insurance",
  "teaser": "Receive your insured items immediately after death!",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/R9be2kXENr7Znt6JtoEaWNzJAQvrIfpQxucNy9uP.png",
  "downloads": 28714,
  "favourites_count": 38,
  "description": "<p>Prapor and Therapist’s teams have been reorganized — they’re now faster and more efficient at recovering your items, delivering them straight to your equipment.</p>\n<hr />\n<blockquote class=\"is-warning\">\n<p><em><strong>NOTICE</strong></em>: This mod processes insurance immediately <em><strong>ONLY AFTER DEATH</strong></em>. When surviving a raid, your items dropped in-raid goes through the <em>regular</em> insurance system.</p>\n<p><em><strong>NOTICE</strong></em>: Be sure to <em><strong>insure</strong></em> the items you want to keep.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr />\n<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Configuration</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><h4>Configuration</h4>\n<p>In the configuration file <code>config.json</code></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>SimulateItemsBeingTaken</code> - If enabled, items can be taken before the insurer can retrieve your item. Chance to keep an item depends on which trader you insured your item from, (Prapor: <code>85%</code>; Therapist: <code>95%</code>, default server settings). Default is <code>true</code></li>\n<li><code>LoseInsuranceOnItemAfterDeath</code> - If enabled, insurance status will be lost on death. Default is <code>true</code></li>\n<li><code>LoseAmmoInMagazines</code> - If enabled, ammo that is loaded into an insured magazine will NOT be kept. Default is <code>false</code></li>\n</ul></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-2\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Installation</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><h4>Installation</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Extract the contents of the .zip archive into your SPT directory</li>\n</ul>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3N6gTe2.gif\" alt=\"Installation\" />\nThank you <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/user/27605/drakiaxyz\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">DrakiaXYZ</a> for the gif</p>\n<h4>Recommended Mods</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Mods that alter insurance prices and/or insurance return percentages. It is recommended to increase insurance prices to balance the changes done by this mod. <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/236/server-value-modifier-svm\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SVM</a> by <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/user/3972/ghostfenixx\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GhostFenixx</a>, and <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/1547/trader-qol\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">TraderQOL</a> by <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/user/41131/mattdokn\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Mattdokn</a> provides options for changing insurance related options</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Compatibility</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested to be compatible with <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2326/project-fika\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Project Fika</a></li>\n<li><strong>Incompatible</strong> with <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2032/nocheese\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">NoCheese</a> as of version 1.0.3</li>\n</ul></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-3\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">FAQs</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><h4>FAQs:</h4>\n<h4>Why am I losing <em><strong>some</strong></em> of my items even though <code>SimulateItemsBeingTaken</code> is <code>false</code>?</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Insurance is processed immediately <em><strong>ONLY AFTER DEATH</strong></em>. When surviving a raid, your items dropped in-raid goes through the <em>regular</em> insurance system</li>\n<li>You can still lose items if they’re uninsured</li>\n<li>Inspect your server logs, they contain information on how your items were processed after the raid ends</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>I’m still losing my items in laboratory, is there a way to change this?</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><code>SimulateItemsBeingTaken</code> is overridden if insurance is disabled on the map. You can use <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/236/server-value-modifier-svm\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SVM</a> by <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/user/3972/ghostfenixx\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GhostFenixx</a> to enable insurance inside laboratory, <code>Raid Settings -&gt; Misc -&gt; Working insurance inside Laboratory</code> is checked</li>\n</ul></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-4\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Support</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><h4>Support</h4>\n<p>If you find bugs, or have feature suggestions, feel free to post them on the comment section, or open an issue on GitHub, or most preferably through the <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://discord.com/channels/875684761291599922/1374428464999829555\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SPT Discord, <code>ozen</code></a></p></div></div></div>\n<hr />\n<h3>Changes from Insurance Plus</h3>\n<p>A huge thank you to <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/user/41131/mattdokn\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Mattdokn</a> for allowing me to continue his work on <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/1545/insurance-plus\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Insurance Plus</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Simulate items being taken. Some items might still get sent by mail when the container that holds the item is taken, but not the item itself</li>\n<li>Uses SPT methods to simulate items being taken, thank you SPT team!</li>\n<li>Ported to the new SPT C# Server</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>If you enjoy my work, you can <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/ozenm\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">buy me a coffee</a> ☕</p>\n<p>\n<em><strong>Policy Notice:</strong> Insurance scamming is not tolerated. Those items dropped in-raid will be processed through the regular insurance system.</em></p>\n",
